<blockquote>
<p>if this pattern opens a portal that usually has stuff that kills people, then how do they know what it vaguely looks like?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Since SCP-259 is computer generated, it's possible to tweak the parameters in the generating program to produce something that is close to the SCP image, but does not have anomalous effects. It's dangerous to try, because you won't know that it won't do anything until you generate it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Also, a dimension filled with spiders has been done before, see SCP-507.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><a href="http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/GiantSpider">Giant spiders</a> are pretty iconic in horror fiction. Would you like giant cockroaches better?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>We already got SCP-508</p>
</blockquote>
<p>OK, we do. SCP-508 is:</p>
<p>&#8212; an autostereogram, which means its effect is entirely based on a trick of human perception<br />
&#8212; non-reproducible, according to the author<br />
&#8212; not very dangerous. The effects are mostly benign/whimsical. The only reason the thing is dangerous is that the scientists didn't let the D-Class leave the room or stop looking at 508 when they saw something disturbing.</p>
<p>I think it's a superficial similarity, and the feel of the article is totally different.</p>

